content.text:
verdict: findings
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1 decidable-without-annex, result: pass, notes: "Asks 1-3 carry enough inline substance to decide; ask 4 is decidable only by trusting an unsourced premise (noted under scenario 4)"}
  - {scenario: 2 first-paragraph-answers, result: pass, notes: "Quote: 'Recommendation: enrich the role-definition typedef with six sections... re-author the three roles through it, and import the skill catalogue by kind'"}
  - {scenario: 3 no-unintroduced-terms, result: pass, notes: "RAPID/DACI, SFIA glossed inline; Scrum and Team Topologies carry functional descriptors; but 'working-mode'/'technique' coinages appear in paragraph 1 and are only explained at ask 3, and 'chain' is never glossed"}
  - {scenario: 4 asks-complete-and-gating-stated, result: fail, notes: "Ask 4 has no evidence element — asks 1-3 each carry a labeled *Evidence:* line, ask 4 asserts the grant's existence and terms with no source; gating for the set IS stated ('Asks 1-3 gate the work; ask 4 defaults on silence')"}
ask_decidability: ["ask 1: confident — six sections and two rules named, failure classes mapped, frameworks cited, default stated (though Default posture is the one section no failure class or framework visibly backs)", "ask 2: confident — order and rationale inline; annex §4 is execution detail, not needed for the decision; small snag that it says 'amended chain' where ask 1 amended a typedef", "ask 3: wobbly — the by-kind disposition and all six working-mode names are inline and approvable, but 6 + ~19 + 8 + 3 + the TDD draft does not visibly reconcile with 'the 36-skill inventory', so I cannot confirm the plan accounts for every skill", "ask 4: wobbly — the handling (bind attribution terms to the technique typedef) is clear and conservative, but the grant itself is unsourced: granted by whom, recorded where, exact terms unquoted; and this ask resolves on silence, which raises the bar for an unverifiable premise"]
overload: "right-sized — four asks, one page, annex genuinely optional for asks 1-2, Deferred section correctly parked"
stumbles: ["re-author `lead-architect`, `lead-po`, and `lead-pm` through the amended chain — ask 1 amended the typedef, not a 'chain'; I had to guess these are the same thing", "each a section ask 1 adds — compressed phrasing; forced a re-read to map the three architect failures onto the six sections", "the 36-skill inventory table — the ask 3 numbers (6 + ~19 + 8 + 3, plus the TDD draft) look like ~37; I stopped to re-add them", "3 ops skills wait for post-migration BC operations — 'BC' arrives abbreviated after 'Bounded Context' was spelled out once in a different ask", "The technique skills exist under a direct author grant requiring preserved attribution — a grant from whom, recorded where?"]
unintroduced_terms: ["chain (asks 2 and 3 — never glossed; presumably shop vocabulary, but a cold reader cannot tell which chain ask 2 means)", "working-mode skills (paragraph 1 — enumerated and made clear only at ask 3)", "technique skills (paragraph 1 — glossed only at ask 3)", "BC (ask 3 — abbreviation never tied to 'Bounded Context')"]
top_changes: ["Give ask 4 a labeled *Evidence:* line naming where the author grant is recorded and quoting its attribution term — it is the only ask without one, its premise is currently unverifiable, and it resolves on silence", "Reconcile the skill arithmetic in ask 3 with the '36-skill inventory' reference — state one exact total and make the five buckets visibly sum to it", "In ask 2, write 'through the amended typedef (v3)' instead of 'through the amended chain' (or gloss which chain), and expand 'BC' at its first abbreviated use in ask 3"]
